# What must never reach the image.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter: `.env` holds the OpenAI key,
# and `output/` holds real people's CVs and transcripts from local runs. A
# `COPY . .` without this file bakes both into a layer that anyone who pulls the
# image can read, and a layer cannot be un-published after the fact.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
output/
uploads/

# Local state and tooling — none of it runs in the container, all of it is weight
# and cache-busting churn.
.git/
.github/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# Tests ship deliberately: `docker compose exec api python -m pytest tests/ -q`
# on the box is the fastest way to tell whether a deploy is sane, and they weigh
# a few hundred KB.
#   tests/  <- intentionally NOT ignored

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Real CVs kept beside the project for manual runs — not fixtures.
*.pdf
!tests/**/*.pdf
